# Phys4D project checklist (required)

This repo tracks implementation against the **May 2026 reframe** (visual dynamics + temporal extrapolation). Do not guess progress from memory.

## At session start

1. Read **`docs/PROJECT_CHECKLIST.md`** (sections A–H).
2. Note which items are `[x]`, `[~]`, or `[ ]` before proposing or implementing work.
3. Prefer tasks from **section H (Next actions)** unless the user redirects.

## At session end (if you changed code, ran experiments, or finished Modal jobs)

1. **Update** `docs/PROJECT_CHECKLIST.md`: flip statuses, fill Notes, add a **Changelog** row (date + one-line summary).
2. If you completed a next-action, check it off in section H and add any new follow-ups.
3. Briefly tell the user which checklist IDs moved (e.g. “C4 partial → x”, “E7 still open”).

## Scope reminders

- **Novelty** = predict frames **60–89** from **0–59**, not only 4DGS reconstruction or camera holdout.
- **3DGS/4DGS** = upstream git (graphdeco, fudan) via Modal; our code = data export, dynamics, eval.
- **L_render** true PSNR is **not done** until E7 is `[x]`; proxy metrics (E6) are not sufficient for the headline claim.

## Do not

- Mark batch 4DGS (C4) done until Modal smoke finished and artifacts downloaded.
- Mark cross-scene dynamics (D6) done until trained/eval’d on full batch with physics holdout.
- Expand scope (system-ID path, physics losses) without user ask — track as `[ ]` in checklist only.
